# 9. ANDROID 16 USB / ADB BAT PROVISIONING WORKFLOW

For Android 16 devices, provide a separate USB/ADB provisioning workflow.

The user must not get access to the BAT file until the customer and device registration form has been completed and validated.

### Workflow

1. User opens Add New Device.
2. User fills all customer details.
3. User fills all device details.
4. Backend validates the account and available entitlement.
5. Backend creates a pending enrollment session.
6. User selects Android 16 USB/ADB provisioning.
7. The dashboard generates a session-specific BAT file.
8. User downloads the BAT file to a Windows computer.
9. User connects the mobile device through USB.
10. User enables Developer Options.
11. User enables USB Debugging.
12. User authorizes the connected computer.
13. User executes the downloaded BAT file.
14. The BAT file checks the ADB environment.
15. It checks device connectivity.
16. It checks USB debugging authorization.
17. It checks the Android version and provisioning prerequisites.
18. It executes only supported provisioning commands.
19. It verifies the expected Device Owner state.
20. The AK DeviceLock application communicates with the backend.
21. Backend validates the pending session and device identity.
22. Registration completes.
23. One entitlement is consumed.
24. Device appears in the correct dashboard.

### BAT file requirements

The generated BAT file must:

- Be unique to the pending enrollment session.
- Contain no permanent private signing keys or reusable secrets.
- Use a short-lived, restricted session token or securely retrieve authorization through the supported workflow.
- Check whether ADB is installed or available.
- Display clear instructions.
- Check device connectivity.
- Check USB debugging authorization.
- Stop when a prerequisite fails.
- Display useful error messages.
- Verify provisioning success.
- Verify Device Owner status.
- Avoid destructive operations.
- Never silently bypass Android security.
- Never report success when provisioning has failed.

### Android 16 technical restrictions

ADB Device Owner provisioning is subject to Android provisioning-state requirements and manufacturer-specific restrictions.

Do not claim that a BAT file can turn any already-configured Android 16 device into a Device Owner-managed device.

If a factory reset, setup-wizard provisioning state, supported QR provisioning or other prerequisite is required, explain it clearly before the user starts.

Test Samsung and other manufacturers individually.

