# 11. REMOTE DEVICE LOCKING SYSTEM

Integrate the existing working Android locking engine into the new platform.

Do not replace it without a documented technical reason.

The backend must support:

- Remote lock
- Remote unlock
- Device status
- Device synchronization
- Device release

### Command workflow

Operator Dashboard

→ Backend authentication

→ Role permission validation

→ Device ownership validation

→ Command creation

→ Command signing

→ FCM notification

→ Device retrieves command through authenticated HTTPS

→ Device validates command signature

→ Device validates command target

→ Device checks expiry and replay protection

→ Existing LockManager executes the operation

→ Device sends acknowledgment

→ Backend updates command and device status

### Command fields

- command_id
- device_id
- command_type
- issued_at
- expires_at
- nonce
- key_id
- signature
- reason
- created_by
- execution_status

FCM must be treated only as a notification mechanism.

FCM delivery alone does not authorize a command.

The device must retrieve and validate the command securely.

### Important rules

- Do not execute expired commands.
- Do not execute replayed commands.
- Do not execute commands for another device.
- Do not execute commands signed by an unauthorized key.
- Do not report success until the device acknowledges actual execution.
- If the device is offline, display Pending/Waiting for Device.
- Authorized unlock and release must remain possible through the supported recovery design.

